INT. BREWERY - COPPER VAT ROOM - NIGHT

Gleaming copper. Pipes. Steam. A catwalk overhead.

WREN (30s, black coveralls, hair under a cap) drops from a ceiling hatch. Soft landing. Duffel on her shoulder.

KOJO (40s, heavy, brewery uniform stolen from a locker) holds the vault dolly. Sweat down his neck.

WREN
Status.

KOJO
Vault's open. Bag's full. Too easy.

WREN
Easy is the plan.

An earpiece crackles. A radio on Kojo's belt hisses.

MAEVE (V.O.)
(radio)
Wren, Kojo. Guard's on his round. Four minutes to the east door.

WREN
Copy, Maeve. Where's the van?

MAEVE (V.O.)
(radio)
Loading dock. Engine warm. Nobody within a block.

KOJO
Told you. Easy.

WREN
Stop saying that.

They wheel the dolly toward the exit. Cash bags stacked like grain sacks. Behind them, a vat gurgles, lazy.

KOJO
We're done. Home by one.

WREN
Quiet.

The east door rattles. A key in the lock.

Wren and Kojo freeze. The dolly stops mid-roll.

MAEVE (V.O.)
(radio)
He's early. Two minutes early. Wren, move.

KOJO
(whispering)
Where?

WREN
Behind the vat.

They duck behind the copper belly. The door swings open. HOLT (50s, security guard, flashlight, thermos) shuffles in, whistling.

He sweeps the beam across the floor. Stops on the dolly tracks in the dust. Follows them. Stops at the vat.

HOLT
Evening, folks.

Wren steps out, hands raised, slow.

WREN
Evening.

HOLT
I've been working this shift eleven years. You're the first people to bother with the copper.

Kojo steps out too. Hands high.

KOJO
We can explain.

HOLT
I'd hope not.

He sets the thermos down. Sits on a crate. Pours himself a cup.

HOLT (CONT'D)
My pension got cut last spring. Did you know that?

WREN
No.

HOLT
They never tell a man until he's already counted on it.

MAEVE (V.O.)
(radio)
Wren? What's happening in there?

Wren looks at Holt. Holt sips his coffee. Looks at the bags. Looks at the open east door.

HOLT
I'm going to finish this cup. Slowly. Then I'm going to walk the north corridor. It takes twelve minutes.

Wren lowers her hands.

WREN
Thank you.

HOLT
Go.

They grab the dolly and run. The east door clicks shut behind them. Holt drinks.

MAEVE (V.O.)
(radio, faint)
Wren? Anyone?

Holt picks up the dropped radio from the floor, thumbs the switch.

HOLT
(into radio)
They're on their way, miss. Drive carefully.
